# Radio fade - short, linear, and over before anyone notices.
#
# What a broadcast desk does between records: no EQ, no beat, no ceremony. Deliberately
# linear rather than equal-power, because on speech and on records that do not overlap
# well the constant-power curve holds both up too long and they collide in the middle.

name    Radio fade
note    a short, plain fade - what a broadcast desk does
align   free
tempo   free
power   free

lane out gain
    at 0.0    1.0    linear
    at 0.5    0.0    hold
    at 1.0    0.0    hold

lane in gain
    at 0.0    0.0    linear
    at 0.5    1.0    hold
    at 1.0    1.0    hold
